From 0d867f1adf7e78328fe11022c19a6da702e044b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wrysk <wrysk@wryskware.dev>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 05:09:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add a read-only per-member flow ledger and its replay
 diagnostic

Diagnostic branch only, based on frozen 512ee52. This is not for main: it exists
so the paid juvenile bottleneck can be measured at the mutation sites instead of
inferred from the 200-tick census in the retained charging artifacts.

crates/cubarium-core/src/flow.rs is a write-only accumulator. Every amount is
read at the assignment that moves it, in the core's own expression, so a tick
that both oxidises and grows is not collapsed into one reserve delta. The growth
predicate is read before the branch it gates, so a closed gate is an observation
rather than the absence of a growth record. Upkeep keeps its three demanded terms
apart from the single clamped debit the core actually pays; splitting that debit
across them would be attribution, not measurement.

world.rs gains one Option field and twelve recording sites, each a null check
when the ledger is absent. The only existing lines changed are the five that name
the growth step's four caps so the binding one can be recorded; the arithmetic and
its order are untouched, and the closing-bytes identity gate proves it.

FlowLedger::probe reconciles the recording rather than trusting it: for every
member and every tick, the stocks the world holds must equal the previous tick's
stocks plus exactly the flows recorded, with the death tick closing against the
removal site. A missed mutation site shows up as a residual.

crates/cubarium/examples/juvenile_flow.rs replays one retained arm behind four
gates: recorded opening sha256 and state hash, replayed closing bytes and state
hash equal to the retained artifact, two replays differing only in
enable_flow_ledger() agreeing on closing bytes and every event record, and zero
reconciliation violations. Output is one record per member plus 60-second bins.

No configuration, threshold, cost, geometry, gate or default moves.

cargo test -p cubarium-core: 149 lib (8 new) plus every integration suite pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
